subject feat(br): enable entropy feedback for q8 and q9

diff --git a/docs/performance/br/command-model-lifetime.md b/docs/performance/br/command-model-lifetime.md
index 8402fc61..9076e8c3 100644
--- a/docs/performance/br/command-model-lifetime.md
+++ b/docs/performance/br/command-model-lifetime.md
@@ -837,3 +837,22 @@ q2 was also measured with an optimal parse (XML 0.6843, dickens 0.9737) but
 was reverted: the incremental q2 contract requires a warmed second encode to
 allocate nothing, and the optimal parser allocates per block. Keeping q2
 lazy-only preserves that streaming guarantee; q3-q7 carry the ratio gains.
+
+q8 and q9 previously ran the optimal parser without entropy feedback, leaving
+them about 1.6% above q10 in absolute bytes. Enabling feedback on both closes
+most of that:
+
+| File | q8 before | q8 after | q9 before | q9 after |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| XML | 4,711 | 4,539 | 4,662 | 4,505 |
+| dickens | 22,766 | 22,412 | 22,742 | 22,387 |
+| webster | 19,858 | 19,574 | 19,838 | 19,556 |
+| nci | 4,388 | 4,238 | 4,347 | 4,203 |
+| x-ray | 42,488 | 42,488 | 42,488 | 42,455 |
+| ooffice | 30,647 | 30,647 | 30,648 | 30,648 |
+
+q8/q9 XML now measure 0.9697/0.9705 and dickens 0.8890/0.8881. Encode time
+rises to 65-253 ms on the affected text rows. Because q8/q9 now enable entropy
+feedback, `applyCommandStateLimit` gates the explicit command-state override on
+the quality tag (q10/q11) rather than on feedback alone, preserving the
+existing rejection contract for q8/q9.
diff --git a/src/br.zig b/src/br.zig
index 31dad4af..ea1bb907 100644
--- a/src/br.zig
+++ b/src/br.zig
@@ -5022,9 +5022,10 @@ fn applyCommandStateLimit(
 ) Error!void {
     if (requested_kib == command_state_default_max_input_kib) return;
     const limit = @as(u32, requested_kib) * 1024;
-    // The command-state candidate uses its own bounded parser; its input
-    // ceiling is independent of the schedule's optimal-parser input cap.
-    if (!schedule.optimal.entropy_feedback or limit > 64 * 1024)
+    // The command-state candidate is a q10/q11 feature. Later presets also
+    // enable entropy feedback, so the quality tag is the precise gate.
+    const supports_command_state = schedule.quality == .q10 or schedule.quality == .q11;
+    if (!supports_command_state or !schedule.optimal.entropy_feedback or limit > 64 * 1024)
         return error.InvalidBlockPlan;
     schedule.optimal.command_state_max_input_len = limit;
 }
